{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join","id":1464227,"title":"So: why join?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-16T15:54:33-07:00","id":1464227,"title":"So: why join?","content":"As has been pointed out elsewhere lately, M20 de-emphasizes the importance of the traditions, conventions, and crafts to a Mage's Magick. In earlier editions, the factions were portrayed as if they held near monopolies on their respective paradigms; but in M20, there's nothing that even hints that you must be akashayana to be a martial artist, a chorister to be a religious devotee, part of the New World Order In order to be an awakened agent, and so on. That leaves the factions primarily as political entities, groups that you join for reasons other than determining what your approach to magick is. Though to be fair, each Tradition, Convention, and Craft has a Focus of its own; and if you differ too much from that, you're not going to be a good fit in that group. Still, a group's approach to magick is no longer the main reason why a mage would join it; if anything, the group Focus has been recast as a reason why someone <i>wouldn't</i> join: if you're an atheist or polytheist, the Celestial Chorus probably isn't going to appeal to you, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> So with the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts stripped of their role as \u201cparadigm gatekeepers\u201d, why join them? I'm not asking that rhetorically; there <i>are</i> good reasons to join up. But what are they? I mean that both generally and specifically: there are general benefits to being a member of a group, <i>any</i> group, that shouldn't be discounted. But there are also benefits that <i>specific</i> groups provide, that should also be considered: what would make a martial artist consider joining the Akashayana, or what might draw a religious devotee to the Celestial Chorus? <br /> <br /> Conversely, what might drive someone away, even if their approach to magick is compatible? Why might a shaman choose <i>not</i> to join the Dreamspeakers, for instance?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T16:54:22-07:00","id":1464231,"title":"","content":"Simple. Training, knowledge and support. Just because you Awakened into Magick doesn't mean you automatically understand how you did it, especially if your Beliefs don't conform to those more obviously magical in nature. Traditions, Conventions and Crafts can provide greater understanding to you without months or even years of trial and error. They can provide you with resources and tools that could be hard or even impossible to get.<br /> <br /> And at the same time, they can provide you with security and protection from other supernaturals as well as a community of like-minded individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T17:01:57-07:00","id":1464233,"title":"","content":"So, let's get some of the bigger ones out of the way first.<br /> <br /> First is Networking or access to the community. So you have awakened and you stumble across a group who have ALSO awakened. Suddenly, you have an invitation to a social institution of people just like you. You have peers, you have people you can discuss your theories as you try to muddle out what the hell your doing when you warp reality. Also, people love to be part of a group. Your no longer John Smith, a random weirdo. You are now John Smith, Agent of the NWO or John Smith, the Shaman or whatever. <br /> <br /> In the same way, you now have people more experienced than you who could show you how to do things. We have an entire <i>library</i> about the thoughts of past masters or the kind of stuff they did. Or what about resources, oh we all chip in a certain amount of resources/quintessence every month and we have a joint workshop we can share for more involved crafting than your home sanctum.<br /> <br /> And then, for some of them, there's networking. If your a Syndicate mage, knowing other people will perhaps give you those connections as you move up various corporate ladders. <br /> <br /> Another option is well, protection and information. Now if a Technocrat Kill Squad is gunning, you might get a tip, and you might have somebody to help get you the hell out. <br /> <br /> Now it should be noted these are just very broad strokes, and they should all be expanded, but lets talk about why you might not want to join the Traditions/Technocracy/Crafts etc.<br /> <br /> The first that I can think of is now you are no longer John Smith, random orphan Willworker sitting in his house, but now your John Smith, Agent of X and so any enemies of X might think about taking you out. Perhaps you object to having to follow the rules of some ancient geezer who can't even come to the material world anymore. Perhaps you got picked up by another brand of supernatural creature or purely mundane group and have loyalty to them rather than some nebulous group who are warring over the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T18:14:49-07:00","id":1464235,"title":"","content":"The traditional reason for joining goes back to the narrative for the Council\u2019s existence in the first place, and how much it works for you will depend on if the Ascension War is still hot in your games.<br /> <br /> When the Order of Reason/Technocratic Union began to rise on the waves of the Enlightenment and Reformation it sent waves through the Awakened communities of Europe. The most influential Awakened in the area, mostly Hermetics, Solificati &amp; proto-Choristers realized that the OoR/TU represented an existential threat. Following a model of their ideologies, they devised the Council of Traditions with its nine seats and purple paradigm, proposed as a unification of all mystic traditions against a common threat (as well as a means of expanding Hermetic influence).<br /> <br /> The reason that anyone joined the Council at all, especially with how flawed it was at its inception was simple: the Order of Reason was on the rise and it was intent on eradicating it\u2019s enemies and leading a Revolution of the Consensus. As the other Awakened felt their power waning they ultimately were given three choices: be destroyed, go into hiding (becoming the crafts), or to join the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions and the so-called Ascension War.<br /> <br /> The Council provided institutional support and integrity for mystical awakened, safe places, resources, masters to train them, students to teach, and even from the inception it understood the necessity of being a big tent organization.<br /> <br /> So for most of history, the reasons to join were simple. Often a young mystic Awakened would be taken under their wing as though that were a law of nature but if they knew enough to make a choice the Council still had notable advantages: protection, organization, and the chance to fight back against the OoR/TU and their tyranny of the world. You didn\u2019t have to join the Traditions but with the Crafts or being independent as the other options, it would be appealing to many, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> The end of the Pogrom, if you use it, could change that. If mystics don\u2019t have the active threat of Technocratic death squads hunting them down (at least no more then any sleeper government\u2019s death square) then they have far more flexibility in their choices and can far more securely reject the Traditions. This could create a setting where the New Council struggles to unite a loosely associated confederation as many of its members simply see no alternative to life other then private pursuits within a world governed by the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T18:32:19-07:00","id":1464238,"title":"","content":"Even without the hot Ascension War, the Technocracy is still a threat to any mage that doesn't want to be a part of the Union. A solo Orphan can't do much about a NWO &quot;recruitment&quot; squad that comes to brainwash you into the Technocratic cause instead of the HITMark sent to assassinate them. Belonging to a group of mages is still valuable post-Pogrom, though it makes the Crafts more viable than they used to be... which is already a thing in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T18:47:29-07:00","id":1464240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join#post1464227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts stripped of their role as \u201cparadigm gatekeepers\u201d, why join them? I'm not asking that rhetorically; there <i>are</i> good reasons to join up. But what are they? I mean that both generally and specifically: there are general benefits to being a member of a group, <i>any</i> group, that shouldn't be discounted. But there are also benefits that <i>specific</i> groups provide, that should also be considered:</div> </div> </div> </div>(specific examples addressed further down)<br /> <br /> Some basic questions - just me brainstorming:<br /> 1) How often is a newly awakened Mage presented with unbiased information about the different factions to inform their choice? How often does a would-be Tradition Mentor say, &quot;You know, you have great potential and, as much as I would want to take credit for your tutelage, I don't want to limit your growth by denying you the world of options. My archenemies, the Technocracy have a lot to offer. Let's compare what I have to teach with their perspective. I hear they have a great Requisition System.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> 2) If the factions acted as Paradigm Gatekeepers, how realistic would it be to have undercover agents who could infiltrate an enemy Construct/Chantry? I know this question will get into the Mind Sphere, Mind Shields and Convention Book: NWO - and that's fine. Virtual Adepts and Etherites posing as Technomancers and participating in Hypertech Projects (casting in concert) in a Technocratic Horizon Realm are easier to imagine than an undercover Technomancer waving wands and throwing bones. There is no &quot;Mystic Convention&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join#post1464227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what would make a martial artist consider joining the Akashayana, or what might draw a religious devotee to the Celestial Chorus?</div> </div> </div> </div>The choice, in each case, allows the student to continue to build on a foundation of knowledge they were interested enough in to devote time to learning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join#post1464227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, what might drive someone away, even if their approach to magick is compatible? Why might a shaman choose <i>not</i> to join the Dreamspeakers, for instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Avatar Storm trashed the Umbra - no, never mind that one. In my own chronicles, a shaman who wants to protect Sacred Lands, perhaps in line with a Seeking their Avatar gave them, might think this more achievable by joining Progenitor - Genegineers or It-X - Macro-technicians to work on sustainable development or building taller buildings to maximize existing land use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join#post1464227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'll try to be systematic. Let's say Azdra, an Orphan has been kicking around for a while and she has gathered some knowledge of the three core factions that are Earth-based; Traditions, Technocracy, DA. She is considering reasons to join or not join each faction:<br /> <br /> Yes Traditions: Sex-Magick. Way more freedom than she would have in the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> No Traditions: They refuse to organize themselves to serve specific service rolls for each other that would give them some chance at winning.<br /> <br /> Yes Technocracy: The Technocracy's Conventions and Methodologies are organized in a way that points toward victory. She could find her niche and do what she's good at, counting on the complimentary skills of Mages in other Methodologies.<br /> <br /> No Technocracy: If she does even the most minor fuckup, she could be brought to Room 101, beaten down, interrogated and brainwashed, with the Conditioning making her a potential danger to people she presently cares about. The Technocracy is so hostile to the right to privacy that if the description of the Sanctum Background were applied, she would still be under surveillance in her five point Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Yes Disparate Alliance: The Bata'a and the Kopa Loei territories are island paradises.<br /> <br /> \u200bNo Disparate Alliance: They are even more poorly organized than the Traditions, who at least have Affinity Sphere specialties (though still no functional roles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-20-2021, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T22:30:24-07:00","id":1464315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes Disparate Alliance: The Bata'a and the Kopa Loei territories are island paradises.<br /> <br /> \u200bNo Disparate Alliance: They are even more poorly organized than the Traditions, who at least have Affinity Sphere specialties (though still no functional roles). </div> </div> </div>Well, The DA is more secret, so the question isn't &quot;should I join the DA&quot; and more &quot;Should I just forget the Traditions and the Technocracy and go my own way, or maybe join these other guys doing their own thing over here,&quot; and later, once they're &quot;in&quot; they discover the network that they use to stay below the Technocracy's radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:15:00-07:00","id":1464344,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming this is from the perspective of an orphan. Because usually mages seek out and help people awaken to usher into their groups. usually it isn't a choice. You are discovered, trained and awakened into your group. And by then your paragrim matches the group that discovered you. So why would you leave.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of good reasons already presented here for those who awaken outside of the groups to join one.<br /> <br /> But I'll present anouther. And that is marauders. Mages fear becoming them, and arguebly anyone who isn't suitably trained is the greatest danger to becoming one because they don't understand their own limitations or paradox. Being an untrained mage is dangerous. your own magic is dangerous. Joining anouther group that can teach you how to controle your own magic is beneficial to you.<br /> <br /> Also arguebly, unless you begin in a group you wouldn't have access to any of the following backgrounds at character creation: Familliar, wonder, node, chantry,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T13:21:12-07:00","id":1464412,"title":"","content":"A point not already addressed is that some groups might be exactly what the mage is looking for. An example might be a mage who really views their Awakening through a Christian lens. It can seem weird NOT to join either the Celestial Chorus or the Templars. Being a part of a community of the faithful is why people join churches in the first place. It can seem counter to the very mentality of one's Focus to avoid joining a group of fellow believers. (For a certain value of fellow believers, in the case of the Chorus.)<br /> <br /> For that matter, any group that is heavily tied to a Real Life religion or ethnic/cultural group will seem like a no-brainer to a person who belongs to that religion or ethnic/cultural group. There can be, if not social pressure (from those few loved ones that are in on your secret), then internalized pressure to join the group of mages made up of &quot;your people&quot;. Dreamspeakers, Bata'a, Ngoma, Kopa Loei, and Sisters of Hippolyta (specifically for descendants of the Amazonian diaspora, which is a thing in WoD) seem particularly appealing for this reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> A different factor is that some groups have proprietary skills or knowledge. The big example I can think of is the Akashayana and their Ur martial art, DO.<br /> <br /> The books are very clear on this point, even in M20. Aside from a vanishingly few not of the Tradition who were trusted with instruction, you cannot learn Do if you are not a part of the Akashayana. Period.<br /> <br /> <br /> While protection from outside forces and the ability to network is a factor, so is just having access to resources that mage groups keep to themselves. When all of the major and minor Nodes in an area are firmly controlled by an established group, and you've got a starving Familiar, you have some tough choices to make. You may also need that Quintessence for less dire, but still important personal reasons. Things like magickal research or creating Wonders. It can be easier to secure the magickal resources you need if you're on the inside. Most mage factions aren't going to just give up access to any random willworker that shows up at their door. Least of all the kind of regular access a mage might require.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:02:51-07:00","id":1464613,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember that one or two of the 2nd edition books implied or stated outright that a lot of Traditions mages were actually brought in through the OoHs attempts to train sleepers. Those who awakened who didn't mesh with Hermetic teachings were then shepherded to other Traditions. I think it might have been the 2nd edition OoH Tradbook. <br /> <br /> I don't think this makes much sense, I'm just pointing it out as an earlier attempt to explain how people find their Traditions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T15:57:52-07:00","id":1464650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464613#post1464613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember that one or two of the 2nd edition books implied or stated outright that a lot of Traditions mages were actually brought in through the OoHs attempts to train sleepers. Those who awakened who didn't mesh with Hermetic teachings were then shepherded to other Traditions. I think it might have been the 2nd edition OoH Tradbook. <br /> <br /> I don't think this makes much sense, I'm just pointing it out as an earlier attempt to explain how people find their Traditions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It makes a great deal of sense. The OoH has the goal of refining Magic so that everyone can learn and awaken. So yes the OoH is committed to teaching the Sleepers. That's why the NWO hates them so deeply. <br /> <br /> And why have a Mage in your order that is bitter because they can't fit in, when you can have an ally in another Tradition that's grateful to you for their early training? The OoH knows how to do politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:11:19-07:00","id":1464654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join#post1464227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been pointed out elsewhere lately, M20 de-emphasizes the importance of the traditions, conventions, and crafts to a Mage's Magick. In earlier editions, the factions were portrayed as if they held near monopolies on their respective paradigms; but in M20, there's nothing that even hints that you must be akashayana to be a martial artist, a chorister to be a religious devotee, part of the New World Order In order to be an awakened agent, and so on. That leaves the factions primarily as political entities, groups that you join for reasons other than determining what your approach to magick is. Though to be fair, each Tradition, Convention, and Craft has a Focus of its own; and if you differ too much from that, you're not going to be a good fit in that group. Still, a group's approach to magick is no longer the main reason why a mage would join it; if anything, the group Focus has been recast as a reason why someone <i>wouldn't</i> join: if you're an atheist or polytheist, the Celestial Chorus probably isn't going to appeal to you, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> So with the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts stripped of their role as \u201cparadigm gatekeepers\u201d, why join them? I'm not asking that rhetorically; there <i>are</i> good reasons to join up. But what are they? I mean that both generally and specifically: there are general benefits to being a member of a group, <i>any</i> group, that shouldn't be discounted. But there are also benefits that <i>specific</i> groups provide, that should also be considered: what would make a martial artist consider joining the Akashayana, or what might draw a religious devotee to the Celestial Chorus?<br /> <br /> Conversely, what might drive someone away, even if their approach to magick is compatible? Why might a shaman choose <i>not</i> to join the Dreamspeakers, for instance?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that was an inherent and important part of Mage from Day 1. It was Revised who had the weird focus that PARADIGMS ARE SPECIFIC IMPORTANT THINGS. Early Mage made it clear everyone knew that will-working was the way things.are.done. Indeed, understanding reality was shaped by your belief was the central reason WHY you Awakened and you never could Awaken unless you understood that Will shapes Reality.<br /> <br /> Indeed, Orphans were an inherently important part of Mage: The Ascension's backstory that I enjoyed as they were people the Traditions scrambled to try to recruit. Because paradigms are MALLEABLE which is another thing that Revised made some questionable assumptions about. You might Awaken because you realized that you could shape reality with your computer but if you met a Choirster, then they might convince you it was really God.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the idea that your Paradigm is some immutable straight jacket you can't change is pretty much my definition of Sorcery. An Order of Hermes mage knows that a Son of Ether, Technocrat, Dreamspeaker, and Hollow One are doing the same thing. He just is aware that his way is BETTER and that he is BETTER at it than them. The same way someone thinks using a computer to calculate sums is better than doing math by hand or thinking about it.<br /> <br /> As why joining? Why not? You get the assistance of mentors, books, and coworkers to help you do it. Yes, you can study all day and night by your lonesome but a mage's journey is one best shared. Certainly, the fascist paramilitary organization that tells you you are going to join them or die might be worth getting some allies against too. So is the guy who thinks that he's seen the true nature of reality and has decided it needs to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:21:08-07:00","id":1464657,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this is one of the aspects of M20 lore I outright ignore.<br /> <br /> If you want to play an Orphan with an adjacent paradigm, you can play an Orphan with an adjacent paradigm. But you're not going to play a Verbena that calls themselves an Iterator. Or an NWO agent who calls themselves Taftani.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:10:37-07:00","id":1464670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464654#post1464654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because paradigms are MALLEABLE which is another thing that Revised made some questionable assumptions about. You might Awaken because you realized that you could shape reality with your computer but if you met a Choirster, then they might convince you it was really God.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the idea that your Paradigm is some immutable straight jacket you can't change is pretty much my definition of Sorcery. An Order of Hermes mage knows that a Son of Ether, Technocrat, Dreamspeaker, and Hollow One are doing the same thing. He just is aware that his way is BETTER and that he is BETTER at it than them. The same way someone thinks using a computer to calculate sums is better than doing math by hand or thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this brings me back to my question: How can a Technomancer-undercover-agent do Mystic Spells in a Tradition Chantry or Node? And if they do so by falling back on Will Working as the underlying principle for which Foci are just an aide, wouldn't playing the cover-role inevitably lead to an abandonment of the Technocratic Paradigm? Technomancers are supposed to be using something that convinces them that what they are doing isn't Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:21:36-07:00","id":1464673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464670#post1464670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this brings me back to my question: How can a Technomancer-undercover-agent do Mystic Spells in a Tradition Chantry or Node? And if they do so by falling back on Will Working as the underlying principle for which Foci are just an aide, wouldn't playing the cover-role inevitably lead to an abandonment of the Technocratic Paradigm? Technomancers are supposed to be using something that convinces them that what they are doing isn't Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>An easy answer would be that you would have one of a few options there:<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocrat agent is one of those rare psychic Technocrats. The ones who don't need foci because they believe they have ESP, telepathy, telekinesis, and so on. They would proceed to do the usual mumbo jumbo but REALLY being using Technomagic.<br /> <br /> 2. The Technocrats would use a brainwashed Order of Hermes, Dreamspeaker, or so on that still has their original magic but has had their loyalties shifted to the Union.<br /> <br /> 3. The Technocrat actually are fully capable of using other Paradigms without issue because quoting 1984 fits with the NWO perfectly.<br /> <br /> To know and not to know, to be conscious of complete truthfulness while telling carefully constructed lies, to hold simultaneously two opinions which cancelled out, knowing them to be contradictory and believing in both of them, to use logic against logic, to repudiate morality while laying claim to it, to believe that democracy was impossible and that the Party was the guardian of democracy, to forget whatever it was necessary to forget, then to draw it back into memory again at the moment when it was needed, and then promptly to forget it again, and above all, to apply the same process to the process itself\u2014that was the ultimate subtlety: consciously to induce unconsciousness, and then, once again, to become unconscious of the act of hypnosis you had just performed. Even to understand the word\u2014doublethink\u2014involved the use of doublethink.<br /> <br /> 4. They impersonate a VA or Son of Ether.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T20:36:24-07:00","id":1464682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464673#post1464673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An easy answer would be that you would have one of a few options there:<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocrat agent is one of those rare psychic Technocrats. The ones who don't need foci because they believe they have ESP, telepathy, telekinesis, and so on. They would proceed to do the usual mumbo jumbo but REALLY being using Technomagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464673#post1464673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The Technocrats would use a brainwashed Order of Hermes, Dreamspeaker, or so on that still has their original magic but has had their loyalties shifted to the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Story-wise, probably the best. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464673#post1464673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Technocrat actually are fully capable of using other Paradigms without issue because quoting 1984 fits with the NWO perfectly.<br /> <br /> To know and not to know, to be conscious of complete truthfulness while telling carefully constructed lies, to hold simultaneously two opinions which cancelled out, knowing them to be contradictory and believing in both of them, to use logic against logic, to repudiate morality while laying claim to it, to believe that democracy was impossible and that the Party was the guardian of democracy, to forget whatever it was necessary to forget, then to draw it back into memory again at the moment when it was needed, and then promptly to forget it again, and above all, to apply the same process to the process itself\u2014that was the ultimate subtlety: consciously to induce unconsciousness, and then, once again, to become unconscious of the act of hypnosis you had just performed. Even to understand the word\u2014doublethink\u2014involved the use of doublethink.</div> </div> </div> </div>NWO, yes. It's a lot of mental gymnastics. This was the first tragedy fiction book that I ever read. I kept thinking Winston and Julia would win somehow. After, I pawned the book of to a friend, telling him it was a heroic love story. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464673#post1464673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. They impersonate a VA or Son of Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> If a building has nine entrances and the bad-guys are always trying to sneak through two of them, a lot more scrutiny is going to be focused on those two. It has the effect of making VAs and Sons of Ether the most suspect Traditions. <br /> <br /> At the moment, I am thinking about crime that happens in Chantries as a wedge for a Syndicate spy to use, but I am drawing a blank as to what kind of crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T20:52:53-07:00","id":1464684,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>How often do Mages Know Each other?</b><br /> <br /> It depends on how you see Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts organized as I've always viewed the Traditions as essentially cell-based rather than something that actually has an organized heirarchy structure, even with the Order of Hermes. It's very possible to be a Son of Ether and stumble upon a Son of Ether chantry that you have never heard of doing an entirely different kind of Science!TM.<br /> <br /> A Mentor gets trained, goes out into the world, finds an apprentice, passes on what he's learned, rince, and repeat often with never taking you to any of the potlucks. The people at Horizon had a list of probably every chantry in the world but they probably know that by asking the Great Gazoo or the Universal Book of EverythingTM that is a literal thing. Its why player characters can have Sennex show up and ask them to investigate Vroomas despite them having no idea who the fuck he is.<br /> <br /> In this case, a Son of Ether or VA could definitely be impersonated but I imagine any REAL Son of Ether or VA would also recognize &quot;Technocrat&quot; magic too so there would be a danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T21:09:54-07:00","id":1464687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464654#post1464654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought that was an inherent and important part of Mage from Day 1. It was Revised who had the weird focus that PARADIGMS ARE SPECIFIC IMPORTANT THINGS. Early Mage made it clear everyone knew that will-working was the way things.are.done. Indeed, understanding reality was shaped by your belief was the central reason WHY you Awakened and you never could Awaken unless you understood that Will shapes Reality.<br /> <br /> Indeed, Orphans were an inherently important part of Mage: The Ascension's backstory that I enjoyed as they were people the Traditions scrambled to try to recruit. Because paradigms are MALLEABLE which is another thing that Revised made some questionable assumptions about. You might Awaken because you realized that you could shape reality with your computer but if you met a Choirster, then they might convince you it was really God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah; but why would the Choristers need to convince him that the computer is really God? It's all just Willworking, after all. <br /> <br /> And no, the focus on paradigms didn't begin in MRev; it didn't even gain any additional attention in Revised. The fact that your Magick conforms to your paradigm was there from the start; and the fact that mages had different views of how Magick works has always been the heart of the Ascension War. That said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464654#post1464654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, the idea that your Paradigm is some immutable straight jacket you can't change is pretty much my definition of Sorcery. An Order of Hermes mage knows that a Son of Ether, Technocrat, Dreamspeaker, and Hollow One are doing the same thing. He just is aware that his way is BETTER and that he is BETTER at it than them. The same way someone thinks using a computer to calculate sums is better than doing math by hand or thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, more or less. The \u201cmore\u201d being that every mage is aware that they have an innate ability to change reality; the \u201cless\u201d being that there's often disagreement as to what the nature of that innate ability <i>is</i>. But yeah; you're spot on about that \u201cstraitjacket\u201d thing: paradigm (or, in M20, Focus) is an aid that helps give the mage some structure to his world-altering ability and prevents him from being rendered impotent by being overwhelmed by the sheer diversity of options at his fingertips; it is <i>not</i> a straitjacket that constrains him. Furthermore, it's not something that's static; through life experiences, one's paradigm can change and grow. <br /> <br /> I <i>will</i> grant that earlier editions phrased the discarding of foci as \u201cgrowing beyond your paradigm\u201d, while M20 describes the Focus as something that one grows <i>into</i> rather than <i>out of</i>; but that's M20 that did that, not MRev. And even in M20, the mystics <i>do</i> know that the Focus isn't <i>necessary</i>; and because of that, they can Work Without Focus. <br /> <br /> But we're kind of getting off topic here. Getting back on topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464654#post1464654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As why joining? Why not? You get the assistance of mentors, books, and coworkers to help you do it. Yes, you can study all day and night by your lonesome but a mage's journey is one best shared. Certainly, the fascist paramilitary organization that tells you you are going to join them or die might be worth getting some allies against too. So is the guy who thinks that he's seen the true nature of reality and has decided it needs to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right; that's been brought up by several people so far: join a group for the safety in numbers and for the comradery. The flip side to that, though, is that once you join up, you've surrendered some autonomy; and mages strike me as the sort of people who tend to cherish their autonomy. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that you're <i>wrong</i>; you aren't. It's just that I don't see joining up with a faction being quite as pervasive in M20 as it was described to be in earlier editions: even in MRev, the assumption was that if you're not a member of a Tradition, Convention, or Craft \u2014 if you're an Orphan \u2014 then your paradigm is a makeshift assortment of tatters, barely functional; what M20 calls Gutter Magic. You join the Choristers in order to have a coherent belief system centered around monotheistic/henotheistic beliefs; you join the Akashic Brotherhood of you want to be a martial artist; and so on. And this notion that Tradition provides paradigm goes all the way back to the first edition. <br /> <br /> But with M20's shift with Orphans so that many of them can and do have fully functional Practices of their own instead of Gutter Magick being practically universal among them, and setting aside the general points about safety and belonging that have been mentioned in this thread so far, why would a religious devotee choose to join the Celestial Chorus? The communal aspect of her beliefs can be satisfied by surrounding herself with fellow believers, true; but I submit that she'd be more likely to find that in fellow believers who happen to be Sleepers than in the Chorus, given the extreme ecumenical nature of the Tradition. <br /> <br /> More generally, I submit that thinking that mages can only get the benefits of fellowship from other mages is part of why some people trend to think that mages isolate themselves from Sleepers. If you change your perspective to allow for the possibility that a mage might be more comfortable around Sleepers who think like him than Awakened who don't, then the groups that mages might align themselves might be Sleeper groups. For instance: an Awakened agent could work for, say, one of the groups described in <b>Project Twilight</b> instead of the NWO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-03-2021, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:13:10-07:00","id":1464717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464673#post1464673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An easy answer would be that you would have one of a few options there:<br /> <br /> 1. The Technocrat agent is one of those rare psychic Technocrats. The ones who don't need foci because they believe they have ESP, telepathy, telekinesis, and so on. They would proceed to do the usual mumbo jumbo but REALLY being using Technomagic.<br /> <br /> 2. The Technocrats would use a brainwashed Order of Hermes, Dreamspeaker, or so on that still has their original magic but has had their loyalties shifted to the Union.<br /> <br /> 3. The Technocrat actually are fully capable of using other Paradigms without issue because quoting 1984 fits with the NWO perfectly.<br /> <br /> To know and not to know, to be conscious of complete truthfulness while telling carefully constructed lies, to hold simultaneously two opinions which cancelled out, knowing them to be contradictory and believing in both of them, to use logic against logic, to repudiate morality while laying claim to it, to believe that democracy was impossible and that the Party was the guardian of democracy, to forget whatever it was necessary to forget, then to draw it back into memory again at the moment when it was needed, and then promptly to forget it again, and above all, to apply the same process to the process itself\u2014that was the ultimate subtlety: consciously to induce unconsciousness, and then, once again, to become unconscious of the act of hypnosis you had just performed. Even to understand the word\u2014doublethink\u2014involved the use of doublethink.<br /> <br /> 4. They impersonate a VA or Son of Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that #4 assumes that the only technomancers in the Traditions are the VAs and Etherites. One thing that <b>Guide to the Traditions</b> did was to highlight how (virtually?) every Tradition includes technomancers in its ranks. Which doesn't <i>solve</i> the \u201cproblem\u201d* of the Traditions tending to assume that technomancers might be infiltrators while mystics probably aren't; but it <i>does</i> extend it beyond <i>just</i> those two Traditions. <br /> <br /> I'd generalize #1 and #4 to \u201cuse a Technocratic Practice that is also Practiced in the group being infiltrated\u201d. I'm not sure that Psionics would be enough, in and of itself, as the Practice of Psionics has its <i>own</i> telltale quirks; but keep that Practice in mind when reading the following:<br /> <br /> Another possibility would be what I'd call the \u201cWizard of Oz\u201d stratagem: have the infiltrator \u201cfake it\u201d using technology. That is, what he's actually doing fits the Technocracy's paradigm; but he's <i>really good</i> at disguising what he's really doing in a way that it <i>looks</i> like he's using the Practice and Instruments of whichever faction he's infiltrating, when he's <i>really</i> using a Technocratic Practice and Instruments. It's tricky to pull off, though not <i>as</i> tricky to pull off as #3 above. Mages don't in general have a special sense that tells them what Practice a mage is using; in terms of sensing Magick, they can sense the <i>Effect</i> but not its <i>cause</i>. And there's likely to be a hubristic assumption that they'd never fall for such a ploy, which ironically means that they might be unusually <i>susceptible</i> to such a ploy. <br /> <br /> Treat it as an unusual application of the Blatancy ability: instead of applying Blatancy to convince Sleepers that the magic they're witnessing is actually science in disguise, the infiltrator applies Blatancy to convince mages that the science in disguise they're witnessing is actually magic. Note that it would be easier to do this if the \u201cscience in disguise\u201d is Psionics, or if the magic that it's being disguised as is technomantic; or both. But while they're <i>easier</i>, they're not the only options. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> * I put \u201cproblem\u201d in scare quotes because is it <i>really</i> a problem for the Technocracy if the Traditions look at a large segment of their own members, including both of the traitorous former Conventions, with distrust? <i>Especially</i> if the infiltration doesn't <i>have</i> to come from that direction. It's classic misdirection: if the Traditions <i>think</i> infiltrators will always be technomancers, they won't be looking for infiltrators who <i>aren't</i> (or at least don't appear to be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:17:32-07:00","id":1464718,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was assuming in the case of 1# that the Technocracy guy would be doing his magic via psionics but shout, &quot;EXPELLIAMUS!&quot; beforehand or whatever he thought Order of Hermes mages did before they pulled out their wands.<br /> <br /> Re: Paradigm<br /> <br /> One thing I always considered was the fact that Traditions might not have always just been the case of HOW people did magic but WHY they did their magic as well. The Technocracy believing they're all Will-Workers doesn't mean they can't believe that Science and Rationality isn't the best way to pursue magic to the point of destroying all other mages. The philosophy of magecraft being worth fighting for among Akashics, Euthanatos, Order of Hermes, and so on.<br /> Certainly, as we see with the Thirty Years War, humans have fought over much less overt differences among practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-21-2021, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:50:45-07:00","id":1464722,"title":"","content":"Of course, I have my own thoughts about Technocrats believing that what they do is Willworking; in a nutshell, I prefer Technocracy Reloaded's approach (where Technocrats acknowledge that what they do messes with reality, but utterly reject the idea that what they do is the same thing as what Superstitionists do). But that's not really relevant here.<br /> <br /> But while \u201cwhy they do their magic\u201d is important, so is the \u201chow\u201d: one thing Malcolm Sheppard pointed out years ago, before the revival of the original World of Darkness, was that his take on the Technocracy in MRev was based on them representing a trap that the intelligent and educated are unusually vulnerable to: e.g., a tendency to put <i>too much</i> faith in scientific models and predictions, and a tendency to want to make reality conform to those models when they fail. He mentioned this to contrast the Technocracy with <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Seers of the Throne, who are a rough analog of the Technocracy but without the tech trappings; and without those trappings, the Seers are \u201cjust\u201d control freaks. Conversely, \u201cthe trap of the Technocracy\u201d gets undermined if they believe that \u201cit's all just Willworking anyway, and how you do it is just window dressing\u201d \u2014 which is why the latter works better as a belief system that's specific to the Traditions, rather than being presented as the setting's gospel truth. <br /> <br /> (It also helps set the Traditions apart from the Disparates, who even in their nascent Alliance are trying to find a way to coexist and cooperate without compromising their various belief systems in the name of some grand pur\u00e9ed blend of \u201cit's all just the same stuff\u201d like what the Traditions peddle.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T23:06:17-07:00","id":1464827,"title":"","content":"I prefer the idea that in Mage, an individual mage's understanding that their power comes from Willworking is <i><b>optional</b></i>. They can be convinced that their Paradigm is the one that's objectively true, and still be perfectly effective at Magick. If anything, the strength of their conviction in the truth of their beliefs arguably should make them <i>better</i> willworkers, because they have no doubt. I say arguably, because I'm not going to commit to that being certain, and there are reasons why this might hamper them.<br /> <br /> For one, you might have a situation like in Dark Ages Mage, where a mage is very good at their particular brand of magick, but have difficulty going outside of it, because their Paradigm doesn't have a model for how they'd begin to attempt it.<br /> <br /> For another, Ascension itself probably requires a transcendental understanding of Magick. You probably can't Ascend if you don't accept that you are Willworking.<br /> <br /> But short of Ascension, a mage should be able to reach the highest tiers of magickal might in this world - Arete 10 - while being convinced of one's Paradigm to the exclusion of all others. The master of their own prison of belief, though a prisoner nonetheless.<br /> <br /> In practice, exposure to the methods and beliefs of other mages conveys some acknowledgement of other Paradigms, if only because to completely discount their existence would require one to slip into Denial Quiets. (Which, admittedly, we have reason to believe some Technocrats have done). The Traditions long ago accepted it as more or less official policy that what mages do is Willworking, though this might be a mix of attempts at inter-Tradition diplomacy and the Order of Hermes forcing their ideas on everyone. Nobody in the Traditions can really go around saying &quot;your belief system is objectively wrong&quot; for political reasons, even if some Traditionalists privately believe it.<br /> <br /> Thing about belief systems is that people have a functionally infinite capacity to rationalize away inconsistencies in their worldviews. They don't need to admit their Paradigm is wrong, and that it really all comes down to Will. They just need to tell themselves that other mages have a functional, if flawed, approach to magick. That there's some loophole, edge case, or unknown mechanism whereby the other mage can do magick without &quot;doing it right&quot;.<br /> <br /> If other mages fall afoul of Paradox, that's just the price they pay for not following the &quot;proper&quot; way. (That the mage themself can also fall afoul of Paradox is a different matter, they would say; or else they chalk it up to having made an error, or being sabotaged by malicious outside agents, or that the proximity to improper mages created bad conditions, or any other convenient excuse).<br /> <br /> Technocrats, to a certain extent, also must acknowledge that Reality Deviants can do what they do. Unlike Traditionalists, though, there's no political incentive to even entertain the notion that mysticism is a valid belief system. To Technocrats, it's obvious that Traditionalists are just doing Science wrong. In truth, I think what Technocrats actually believe varies between Union members. Some might believe that Willworking is a thing - in whatever manner they explain how that works - and they just don't talk about it out loud on the regular (because no one wants to be seen giving credit to Reality Deviants or questioning the validity of Enlightened Science). Others come up with all sorts of pet explanations for mystic practices (that rationalizing again). As mentioned above, some Technocrats go into Denial, rejecting the very idea that mystics can even do Magick at all.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Technocracy has habitually used Conditioning to enforce Union dogma only further muddies the waters. Even thinking that mysticism could have a grain of truth may, depending on level of Conditioning, be <i>literally</i> unthinkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T23:53:02-07:00","id":1464829,"title":"","content":"RE Technocrat Infiltrators of the Traditions<br /> <br /> First, in addition to Psionics or hiding technomatic methods (the &quot;Wizard of Oz&quot; tactic), it's worth remembering that other forms of Technocratic Practice use the same Instruments as Traditionalists.<ul><li>Martial Arts: A Technocrat doesn't need to believe in Chi or other &quot;mystic gobblygook&quot; to scientifically employ martial arts forms, breathing exercises, meditation, and other techniques.</li> <li>Alchemy/Herbalism/Chemistry: Fluids, powders, pills, and solvents look the same to most observers, regardless of whether you're deriving them from arcane sources or synthesizing them in a lab. Herbs are common to both Verbana witches and Progenitor pharmacopists.</li> <li>Art of Desire/Hypereconomics: When it comes to charming the pants off someone, it can be difficult to know what the mage is doing to accomplish it. Art of Desire is a Practice as old as it is subtle.</li> <li>Mathematics/Physics: Aside from the visible application of mathematics looking fairly indistinguishable between arcane and hypertech, to the uninitiated, a suitably intelligent infiltrator could simply do a bunch of calculations in their head (possibly with the aid of a BMI or just years of mental training) to pull off some stunt. A stunt they can then blame on anything from a lucky charm or enchanted weapon to a blessing from God/the spirits/etc.</li> </ul><br /> Second, due to the ever-present threat of Paradox, mages of all stripes are accustomed to seeing their peers go to great lengths to disguise the true source of their magick. Actions taken to establish Coincidence in observers can just as easily be turned to hiding the use of technomancy. So long as a mage carries the trappings of their supposed mystic Practice, they can earn broad tolerance for the Procedures they employ. (That their trinkets might have covert devices hidden within them is almost besides the point).<br /> <br /> Moreover, the beauty of Coincidental magick is that it can be so subtle, even Awakened observers may have trouble telling if anything magickal happened at all. (Barring the correct use of Awakened senses, obviously).<br /> <br /> <br /> (Obviously, any infiltration attempt will rely on the infiltrator avoiding people who would know better. Or knowing enough about the Focus they're trying to fake to pass casual inspection. If a Technocrat spy, pretending to be an Akashic, is the only &quot;Akashic&quot; in the area, there's no one around who can call their bullshit. Even bullshit, though, can be passed off as a weird variant from a distant place in a pinch, and pretending to be a novice can give a spy wider tolerance for unusual application of Practice or strange stated beliefs. Older members of &quot;their Tradition&quot; may even elect to coach the spy, allowing them to hone their disguise further. It's a dangerous gambit, to be sure, but rewarding if you can pull it off.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Third, Technocratic Conditioning can allow a spy to exist within the Traditions who, for all intents and purposes, is a True Believer. Just one that has programming hidden in the back of their head, that activates under certain conditions. The most basic would be programming that makes the spy go off and covertly pass along information they've learned. Every week, the mage loses a few minutes of time, during which they've found a phone and made a report.<br /> <br /> Another bit of programming might be to prevent them from knowingly harming Union personnel. They might have a Technocrat at the end of a gun, but at the last moment feel compelled to jerk slightly away as they fire. As far as anyone - including themselves - knows, they just missed, giving the Technocrat a chance to get away.<br /> <br /> You could build an entire character arc out of a PC slowly realizing they may be Manchurian Candidate. (Personally, I'd prefer that to be something the player opts into when they make the character. No one likes to learn the character they made was a Technocrat the whole time, if the Storyteller made that decision for them.)<br /> <br /> The advantage of the Conditioned character is that their understanding of how magick works is somewhat moot. They can follow a mystical Focus, because the character on the surface believes in a Traditional Paradigm. But they still serve Technocratic interests. They may even have a duel personality, one mystic and one Technocrat, with the latter coming to the fore as needed. (This is another place where I'd leave it to the player to roleplay that disconnect, and even have a second character sheet - or at least Focus description - for their Technocrat alter ego).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T08:15:44-07:00","id":1464874,"title":"","content":"Increasingly I'm of the opinion that not only is joining the Traditions or Technocracy not the obvious choice for new mages, recruiting the randomly awakened is not the obvious choice for the Traditions and Technocracy. It is a large expediture of time and effort to protect and train a new Mage from scratch, and I suspect for the most part they fill their ranks with those who awaken already most of the way into the paradigm. <br /> <br /> That's not to say there is no effort in finding the blank slates, but in my headcanon it is not an active effort. Instead the various efforts to seed Sleeper society has the bonus effect of attracting the newly awakened with the right leanings. These would be things like networks of martial arts studios, secret societies, and free energy social media groups.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one of the games I've wanted to run for a while is one where a bunch of newly awakened have to figure out their magic and find paradigms and mentors on their own. While I originally imagined it as a variant, I think it is significantly more common than I first thought.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T14:11:49-07:00","id":1464910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464874#post1464874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Increasingly I'm of the opinion that not only is joining the Traditions or Technocracy not the obvious choice for new mages, recruiting the randomly awakened is not the obvious choice for the Traditions and Technocracy. It is a large expediture of time and effort to protect and train a new Mage from scratch, and I suspect for the most part they fill their ranks with those who awaken already most of the way into the paradigm.<br /> <br /> That's not to say there is no effort in finding the blank slates, but in my headcanon it is not an active effort. Instead the various efforts to seed Sleeper society has the bonus effect of attracting the newly awakened with the right leanings. These would be things like networks of martial arts studios, secret societies, and free energy social media groups.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one of the games I've wanted to run for a while is one where a bunch of newly awakened have to figure out their magic and find paradigms and mentors on their own. While I originally imagined it as a variant, I think it is significantly more common than I first thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I would disagree but also highlight the differences in position:<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Avatar Storm</b>: The Technocracy will make an effort to recruit and re-train Orphan Mages with a &quot;carrot and stick&quot; approach as a general rule. The carrot is that they'll offer you a six figure salary (at the start) and plenty of talk about helping the world as well as enriching your gift. The stick approach is that they will UTTERLY DESTROY YOUR life so that you end up a pedophile wanted by the police with no money, social security number, or prospects. Very much the Matrix and <i>Nowhere Man</i> if anyone remembers that Bruce Greenwood show. They have the resources to retrain you by either sending you to a Mage college or Room 101.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are going to recruit Orphans because they are on the backfoot with the Technocracy and every single soldier counts. The Traditions actually exist because they are there to provide resources for people to be able to practice their magic in peace so there's no point in not doing it. There's always a need for a new one because there's a couple of thousand of each Tradition in the world and extinction is a very real possibility.<br /> <br /> Plus there's the fact that if you DON'T recruit the Orphan then the Union or Traditions will or, worse, they might become a Marauder or Nephandi. Because the Nephandi will ALWAYS be on the lookout for the ignorant.<br /> <br /> <b>Post-Avatar Storm</b>: Well, things are up in the air, aren't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:08:14-07:00","id":1464916,"title":"","content":"There's more of a divide than before the Avatar storm and after the avatar storm. There is also, for example, long after the avatar storm. But I'm not sure that that makes as big of a difference as you might suppose.<br /> <br /> Note that M20's reinterpretation of orphans does not portray it as a new development. Rather, the idea is that the old interpretation of orphans being ignorant and vulnerable was and is a stereotype.<br /> <br /> Note also that the security that comes with joining the traditions or crafts is more theoretical than practical. How often has your cabal been able to call in reinforcements from other parts of the traditions and been able to rely on them? Usually, they have their own problems to deal with.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that you never get help; that it may not be as big a boon as you might at first suppose.<br /> <br /> And finally, it has been suggested at several places in the text that the technocracy isn't as all powerful as it appears to be. So the idea that they're an ever-present threat that <i>will</i> snatch up any \u201cwandering Orphan\u201d (again with that stereotype) and brainwash them is almost certainly an exaggeration. Of course, if the technocracy actually has caught wind of a particular orphan and is out to get him or her, then that's a moot point: it doesn't matter if it \u201chardly ever happens\u201d if it's happening to you.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> In short, I'm going with Brucato's idea, outlined in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>, is optional: the technocracy and traditions aren't so omnipresent that every newly awakened mage will find themselves inducted into the war. And that's not coming from the mage revised crew; that's coming from the guy who was in charge all through first and second editions.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind: let's say that you have thus far managed to avoid the Ascension war; heck, let's even assume that you're living in a lull in the Ascension War, such as the early part of MRev (after the Avatar Storm caused the Technocracy to back off but before they went gunning for the Crafts). Why would you join a Tradition? That is, what non-\u201cAscension War\u201d reasons are there for joining up? Another poster mentioned that one perk of joining the Akashayana is access to Do, of which that Tradition has a near-monopoly; and if it's all that it's cracked up to be, that might be a reason to join instead of just developing your own martial arts. What about the other Traditions? What selling points do they have in a market where it isn't, in effect, \u201cjoin someone or die\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:56:13-07:00","id":1464929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464874#post1464874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, one of the games I've wanted to run for a while is one where a bunch of newly awakened have to figure out their magic and find paradigms and mentors on their own. While I originally imagined it as a variant, I think it is significantly more common than I first thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just looking at Devotional Resonance, I noticed Patriotism as one of the descriptors. Mages might organize around the collective interests of a specific population. Alternatively, consider the movement for The Rights of Nature, a legal concept that a lake or mountain has a right to exist. This is actually gaining ground. As a concept for a Chronicle, there is a lot of metaphysics that could be applied to a body of water around which a city is built. It could start with someone discovering a way to communicate with the lake or river and then going on a Deep Umbral mission to the Fortress of Government with an important mission. Stuff to play around with. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3zHci0QogQU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3zHci0QogQU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3zHci0QogQU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3zHci0QogQU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kuFNmH7lVTA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kuFNmH7lVTA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kuFNmH7lVTA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kuFNmH7lVTA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.macleans.ca/society/environment/why-lake-erie-has-the-same-rights-as-a-person-in-toledo-ohio/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.macleans.ca/society/envi...n-toledo-ohio/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T07:44:15-07:00","id":1465010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464829#post1464829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Technocrat Infiltrators of the Traditions<br /> <br /> First, in addition to Psionics or hiding technomatic methods (the &quot;Wizard of Oz&quot; tactic), it's worth remembering that other forms of Technocratic Practice use the same Instruments as Traditionalists.<ul><li>Martial Arts: A Technocrat doesn't need to believe in Chi or other &quot;mystic gobblygook&quot; to scientifically employ martial arts forms, breathing exercises, meditation, and other techniques.</li> <li>Alchemy/Herbalism/Chemistry: Fluids, powders, pills, and solvents look the same to most observers, regardless of whether you're deriving them from arcane sources or synthesizing them in a lab. Herbs are common to both Verbana witches and Progenitor pharmacopists.</li> <li>Art of Desire/Hypereconomics: When it comes to charming the pants off someone, it can be difficult to know what the mage is doing to accomplish it. Art of Desire is a Practice as old as it is subtle.</li> <li>Mathematics/Physics: Aside from the visible application of mathematics looking fairly indistinguishable between arcane and hypertech, to the uninitiated, a suitably intelligent infiltrator could simply do a bunch of calculations in their head (possibly with the aid of a BMI or just years of mental training) to pull off some stunt. A stunt they can then blame on anything from a lucky charm or enchanted weapon to a blessing from God/the spirits/etc.</li> </ul><br /> Second, due to the ever-present threat of Paradox, mages of all stripes are accustomed to seeing their peers go to great lengths to disguise the true source of their magick. Actions taken to establish Coincidence in observers can just as easily be turned to hiding the use of technomancy. So long as a mage carries the trappings of their supposed mystic Practice, they can earn broad tolerance for the Procedures they employ. (That their trinkets might have covert devices hidden within them is almost besides the point).<br /> <br /> Moreover, the beauty of Coincidental magick is that it can be so subtle, even Awakened observers may have trouble telling if anything magickal happened at all. (Barring the correct use of Awakened senses, obviously).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that NWO Greysuits who infiltrate the Traditions also have this technique where they come up with tens of reasons and excuses why they are not using their Magick. Paradigm and approach (&quot;only in the direst circumstances...&quot; &quot;only if there is a real need...&quot; etc.), fear of Paradox, other responsibilities and goals...Then they put a positive spin on this, so they are seen as a careful, reserved Mage who does not use Magick without very careful consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:10:16-07:00","id":1465042,"title":"","content":"I would see Syndicate InSpectors developing an inhouse version of Certamen to practice for the purpose of infiltrating Chantries. An Elitist Personal Paradigm that focuses on competition is easily adapted to the undercover role of a member of Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> To think of an appropriate acronym...<br /> <br /> High Umbral Breach Reconnaissance &amp;Intelligence System (HUBRIS)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-05-2021, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T15:15:33-07:00","id":1465048,"title":"","content":"Since you mentioned the syndicate, may I point out that in addition to being the Convention that's most likely to pass for Sleepers, they may also well be the convention most likely to pass as mystics. Not on the whole, mind you (although some of their Entropy Adjustments can sell pretty mystical); but they have (or had?) one Division that specialized in the weird; an infiltrator outfitted by SPD would arguably be better equipped to pull off a deception than most. (Especially if you go with my version of SPD, which doesn't have Wyrm taint built in.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:20:18-07:00","id":1465056,"title":"","content":"While real world examples can be fraught and all...<br /> <br /> Consider Gwyneth Paltrow. Is she a Tradition mage trying to mainstream alternatives to the Technocratic lifestyle? Or is she a Technocrat making quackery look like stupid rich people wastes of money to the majority of people that react to Goop in any number of negative ways?<br /> <br /> Because the fact that it's not something you could easily say one way or the other over is easily where infiltration can occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:23:27-07:00","id":1465057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1465056#post1465056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While real world examples can be fraught and all...<br /> <br /> Consider Gwyneth Paltrow. Is she a Tradition mage trying to mainstream alternatives to the Technocratic lifestyle? Or is she a Technocrat making quackery look like stupid rich people wastes of money to the majority of people that react to Goop in any number of negative ways?<br /> <br /> Because the fact that it's not something you could easily say one way or the other over is easily where infiltration can occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact Tradition and Technocrat mages can do things against their stated ideology. Gwyneth Paltrow the Syndicate mage may sell crap just to get rich, especially in Revised where there's significantly less oversight.<br /> <br /> No one is going to execute her for running a snake oil business when CONTROL is gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:54:23-07:00","id":1465063,"title":"","content":"According to Syndicate Revised, \u201csnake oil\u201d is and always has been part of the Syndicate playbook. In particular, see the section in there about the various Traditions, and how the Syndicate attempts to sell them stuff, with the end-game being Traditionists who willingly do the Syndic's bidding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T19:01:28-07:00","id":1465081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1464910#post1464910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I would disagree but also highlight the differences in position:<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Avatar Storm</b>: The Technocracy will make an effort to recruit and re-train Orphan Mages with a &amp;quot;carrot and stick&amp;quot; approach as a general rule. The carrot is that they'll offer you a six figure salary (at the start) and plenty of talk about helping the world as well as enriching your gift. The stick approach is that they will UTTERLY DESTROY YOUR life so that you end up a pedophile wanted by the police with no money, social security number, or prospects. Very much the Matrix and <i>Nowhere Man</i> if anyone remembers that Bruce Greenwood show. They have the resources to retrain you by either sending you to a Mage college or Room 101.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That\u2019s the image I got when I first got into Mage, yes. It hasn\u2019t held up very well for me over the years. It works very well when the main antagonist faction is omnipresent, dehumanizing, monolithic, has a long reach nigh infinite resources and a win-at-all-costs attitude. That certainly matches the original black hat Technocracy, and it matches a Traditions that is deeply underground and on the run at almost every turn.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t match the more toned down, long on influence shorter on power Technocracy. It doesn\u2019t match a Traditions that is active in pushing ideas into the popular consciousness. You can\u2019t have publishing battles in the halls of academia, or grass roots organizers vs corporate gentrifiers if the Technocracy is so free-handed with its identity destroying powers. The underdogs couldn\u2019t remain in place long enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T19:54:36-07:00","id":1465086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1465081#post1465081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That\u2019s the image I got when I first got into Mage, yes. It hasn\u2019t held up very well for me over the years. It works very well when the main antagonist faction is omnipresent, dehumanizing, monolithic, has a long reach nigh infinite resources and a win-at-all-costs attitude. That certainly matches the original black hat Technocracy, and it matches a Traditions that is deeply underground and on the run at almost every turn.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t match the more toned down, long on influence shorter on power Technocracy. It doesn\u2019t match a Traditions that is active in pushing ideas into the popular consciousness. You can\u2019t have publishing battles in the halls of academia, or grass roots organizers vs corporate gentrifiers if the Technocracy is so free-handed with its identity destroying powers. The underdogs couldn\u2019t remain in place long enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, they can if they have a cover. You presumably would have Order of Hermes and Choirsters fighting the Ascension War with ideas from cover identities. I was always confused why these weren't a bigger thing in the game.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy can't find you, it can't take you down.<br /> <br /> And yes, there's the period where they haven't identified you as a Mage yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T21:57:43-07:00","id":1465094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1465048#post1465048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you mentioned the syndicate, may I point out that in addition to being the Convention that's most likely to pass for Sleepers, they may also well be the convention most likely to pass as mystics. Not on the whole, mind you (although some of their Entropy Adjustments can sell pretty mystical); but they have (or had?) one Division that specialized in the weird; an infiltrator outfitted by SPD would arguably be better equipped to pull off a deception than most. (Especially if you go with my version of SPD, which doesn't have Wyrm taint built in.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009152-spd-a-new-take\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...spd-a-new-take</a><br /> <br /> Good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T05:18:41-07:00","id":1465120,"title":"","content":"I assume the primary point of joining the Traditions for young Mystics would be to actually be able to advance as Mages at a reasonable rate. I find the idea of Orphans reaching more than 2 (or maybe 3) in any Sphere (or equivalent, if we are assuming Orphans do not use Spheres) to be very much at odds with how the setting of MtA is outlined. The 1st edition Corebook Magick section has in-setting introductions by a Mage tutor welcoming an Initiate and talking about a particular Sphere a bit. The impression these parts give to me is that Magick requires rigorous study, extreme efforts of comprehension and will, considerable perception and outlook shifting, and lots of time and hard work. The Correspondence section says outright that many Mages never attain Correspondence 2 (I assume it refers to Mages who attempt to study Correspondence Magick). Libraries and mentors are mentioned very often, as are debts owed for Magickal tutelage. If raising magickal capabilities was that easy, then why are the majority of Tradition Mages willing to submit to the extensive and often harsh obligations of being Apprentices and following mentors?<br /> Another reason to join Traditions (or other Mage factions) - becoming more skilled in Magick Effects and widening their repertoire of them. And learning Rotes.<br /> <br /> Of course, some Orphans would be the exception to this and able to grow wiser, stronger, and more potent by themselves or with limited contact with other Mages. But I think that such Orphans are extremely rare.<br /> <br /> I have to say that I find the idea of a sizeable number of Orphans kind of confusing. As far as I understand it, the vast majority of Mages are either former Acolytes and Consors, or were Sleepers who caught the attention of a Mage and were led into Awakening. A good example of this is in the first Verbenae Tradition book - the Verbenae kidnap several persons, introduce them to their Paradigm, history, and outlook, and then lead them to Awakening, and these new Mages join the Tradition straight away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-24-2021, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T06:00:05-07:00","id":1465128,"title":"","content":"We're well beyond what the first edition had to say on the subject. These days, the amount of study that it takes to develop your Arete and Spheres depends to a large extent on your Focus: some, like those found among the Order of Hermes or Sons of Ether, rely heavily on study; others, like those featuring Shamanism or Ecstatics or Faith, place more weight on some sort of supernatural revelation, something that <i>can't</i> be taught. In M20 in particular (which is the context of this thread), the idea that Orphans have a rougher time of it exists in precisely one form: that the Practice of Gutter Magic is more common among Orphans than nearly any mage faction (with the Hollow Ones being the noodle exception, in that they embraced Gutter Magic and raised it to an art form). In supporting material for M20, we're given a number of sample mages; and in that sample, most have either never heard of the Traditions or have chosen not to join them. (The martial artist, in particular, specifically did not join the Akashayana, and has philosophical disagreements with them.)<br /> <br /> And the \u201cmost mages are former consors or acolytes\u201d thing is also, at best, a relic of the first edition that has largely been left by the wayside. The Hermetic effort to teach sorcery as a path toward Awakening is generally presented as a mixed bag, with no conclusive proof that it actually works well enough to be worth the effort. Primers are a thing; but they basically nudge someone who's already almost there across the starting line. The impression I get is that most Awakenings are spontaneous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T08:26:55-07:00","id":1466465,"title":"","content":"I get that impression as well, though early on I made the mistake of thinking spontaneous was the same a blank slate. I realized later on that the increased likelihood of strange and supernatural occurrences in a future Mage's life was a seed for planting paradigm preferences and establishing where he would go looking for answers once awakening happened.<br /> <br /> Now I do still think that Tradition actions are responsible for quite a few people awakening with the right predilections and clues to find their way into the Traditions, but I think that's a happy accident. The primary goal is seeding ideas among the sleepers.<br /> <br /> Though, truth be told, I'm not sure if they can say with any certainty how effective their seeding efforts are with sleepers either...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:45:16-07:00","id":1466552,"title":"","content":"Of the first three game-lines, Mage has one of the most versatile systems for creating the backstory of how the splat-character came to join.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, you sink your fangs into someone's body-part-you-prefer and turn them into what you are. Some guidance afterwards is helpful if you want this neonate to do you proud.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, you produce offspring and keep an eye on the bloodline waiting for the recessive gene to manifest.<br /> <br /> The first is direct. The second is somewhat indirect.<br /> <br /> Mage can be anywhere in between. Mages try to propagate their ideas in sleeper society so that some will Awaken and be drawn toward their Paradigm (comparable to Werewolves mating and waiting). Mages can also take a direct approach, selecting a worthy sleeper and coaching them toward Awakening or even attempting to force an Awakening with drastic, Vulgar methods (comparable to Vampires). I don't care if one edition of MtA emphasizes one approach over the other. I am for all of these approaches being available to player backstory and in-game recruitment efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:52:15-07:00","id":1466573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466465#post1466465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that impression as well, though early on I made the mistake of thinking spontaneous was the same a blank slate. I realized later on that the increased likelihood of strange and supernatural occurrences in a future Mage's life was a seed for planting paradigm preferences and establishing where he would go looking for answers once awakening happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>In practical terms most people already have their own Paradigms anyway. They have a notion, albeit a lose one, of how reality works, how it should work, and how they can affect it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466552#post1466552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage can be anywhere in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a third option, where you became a Mage by yourself without any strong influence from other Mages, just because the spark of it isn't inherited from another one, but an inherent human capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:06:11-07:00","id":1466578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466573#post1466573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a third option, where you became a Mage by yourself without any strong influence from other Mages, just because the spark of it isn't inherited from another one, but an inherent human capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, true. I forgot that one. One of my players is an Orphan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:25:24-07:00","id":1466583,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I'm an outlier or not but the absolute vast majority of my and my groups chronicles over the years have been Orphan games that rarely reached Arete 3, I can probably count on one hand the number of times that PCs chose to join larger organisations, whether traditions or conventions...Crafts were slightly more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:32:03-07:00","id":1466585,"title":"","content":"No offense intended; but given the nature of this thread, that's a big oversight. Because Brucato has taken the stance that that's where the majority of Awakening's come from: not the actions of the Traditions/other mages, but spontaneous Awakenings. <br /> <br /> The most that mages typically contribute is their efforts to seed the culture with ideas compatible with Awakening, putting the building blocks necessary for constructing a Focus that's rugged enough to be used for Willworking. But the actual spark that's needed to Awaken isn't something they can trigger, for the most part. And without a reliable means of triggering an Awakening, they have to disseminate their ideas as far and wide as possible in order to have enough of a chance of equipping someone to Awaken to make the effort worthwhile. <br /> <br /> But the further you spread your ideas, the harder it is to monitor those who receive them and if you spread them far enough to have a decent chance of Awakening one mage, chances are <i>really</i> good that that new mage will Awaken somewhere that you're not watching. Because even the NWO doesn't have that extensive of a monitoring operation. <br /> <br /> In short: if Embraces are direct and Garou breeding is somewhat indirect, Awakenings tend to be <i>extremely</i> indirect, to the point that drawing a connection between Mage efforts to encourage Awakenings and the Awakenings themselves is nearly impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:46:34-07:00","id":1466589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466583#post1466583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if I'm an outlier or not but the absolute vast majority of my and my groups chronicles over the years have been Orphan games that rarely reached Arete 3, I can probably count on one hand the number of times that PCs chose to join larger organisations, whether traditions or conventions...Crafts were slightly more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if an outlier <i>per se</i>. I've noticed already that people have very diverse experiences with Mage. I know others that rarely or never associate with any large organization and stay as Orphans or Craft members. Others that <b><u>never</u></b> played an Orphan or Craft member or saw one as PC.<br /> <br /> Which one is more common, I don't know. I would guess it is the later, but that's just a guess, and both are definitely common enough that I wouldn't call any of them an outlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466585#post1466585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short: if Embraces are direct and Garou breeding is somewhat indirect, Awakenings tend to be <i>extremely</i> indirect, to the point that drawing a connection between Mage efforts to encourage Awakenings and the Awakenings themselves is nearly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an analysis of the setting it is reasonably correct, but as an analysis of a character option it isn't.<br /> <br /> Even if the Order of Hermes is wrong that their initiation process for Sleepers actually increase their chances at Awakening, from the PoV of one such apprentice it matters little. They Awakened in their care and definitely got their Paradigm from them.<br /> <br /> The same goes for the &quot;indirect&quot; route. For an initiate in a Tradition that felt their influence before the Awakening and got their attention early, what does it matters if this was actually a coincidence? As a character concept it's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:12:46-07:00","id":1466596,"title":"","content":"To update my blurb: I am for all of these approaches being available to player backstory <i>including spontaneous Orphan Awakenings</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T07:36:15-07:00","id":1466648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1466585#post1466585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most that mages typically contribute is their efforts to seed the culture with ideas compatible with Awakening, putting the building blocks necessary for constructing a Focus that's rugged enough to be used for Willworking. But the actual spark that's needed to Awaken isn't something they can trigger, for the most part. And without a reliable means of triggering an Awakening, they have to disseminate their ideas as far and wide as possible in order to have enough of a chance of equipping someone to Awaken to make the effort worthwhile.<br /> <br /> But the further you spread your ideas, the harder it is to monitor those who receive them and if you spread them far enough to have a decent chance of Awakening one mage, chances are <i>really</i> good that that new mage will Awaken somewhere that you're not watching. Because even the NWO doesn't have that extensive of a monitoring operation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I mean. Most awakenings are spontaneous, but that doesn't mean they are completely blank slates paradigm wise. If Mages can't control when, where, or even whom awakens, they need to influence where the newly awakened look for answers. There's a lot of forms this can take, such as keeping a presence on chat rooms, maintaining secret societies, etc. but conveniently, most of these are things they already want to do in their efforts to manipulate the consensus.<br /> <br /> Now I'm sure there is a debate within the Traditions about if these efforts are leading to new awakenings or just influencing the paradigm leanings of spontaneous awakenings, but that largely doesn't change much about their actions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T09:18:57-07:00","id":1466657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464227-so-why-join?p=1465128#post1465128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're well beyond what the first edition had to say on the subject. These days, the amount of study that it takes to develop your Arete and Spheres depends to a large extent on your Focus: some, like those found among the Order of Hermes or Sons of Ether, rely heavily on study; others, like those featuring Shamanism or Ecstatics or Faith, place more weight on some sort of supernatural revelation, something that <i>can't</i> be taught. In M20 in particular (which is the context of this thread), the idea that Orphans have a rougher time of it exists in precisely one form: that the Practice of Gutter Magic is more common among Orphans than nearly any mage faction (with the Hollow Ones being the noodle exception, in that they embraced Gutter Magic and raised it to an art form).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think agree on spirit, but I would contend that Shamanism, Ecstatics or Faith IRL have a long lasting tradition of gurus, complex practices that require teaching, oral tradition...that a corpus of knowledge doesn't rely on academics doesn't mean that it can't heavily benefit from masters, institutions, <b>practice </b>that the Factions provide by virtue of having a large number of *practicioners* (One could debate if that can be called &quot;studying&quot;, but I understood that argument not solely as the advantage of &quot;hitting the books&quot;, but the advantage of learning magick from others in general)<br /> <br /> The fact that Grimoires are a thing means that study has mechanical advantages, even in M20. And I'm all for &quot;alternate&quot; types of Grimoires that aren't books (like the &quot;oral tradition&quot; example in FbDF, that can easily be ported as virtual wonders) so I don't think those Paradigms you mention should be <i>devoid </i>of the advantages of &quot;studying&quot;.<br /> <br /> The rules of XP remained as the 1rst source of Sphere levels, but there were always outliers. Grimoires, the rules of Tradition's Guide, whatever they had in 1e - were rarely used in my experience, but were there.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the <i>setting </i>seems to assume it's important in one way or anoother. No other WoD game has a Library backgound. More so, teaching and learning were always a big thing in the Lore: The whole &quot;apprentice - master&quot; relationship that's both in the rules as an aesthetical choice and in the lore as a <i>social mechanic </i>important for many mage characters.<br /> <br /> I would say that taking ALL of Mage into consideration, learning from Mentors (and other ways of assisted learning) was always a thing and still is.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER as an advantage it was always a fuzy thing, and I wouldn't go so far as what <i>Muad'Dib </i>statted of Orphans not reaching further than 3 dots in Spheres. The posibility to be entirely self-reliant was (too) always there (whith the whole your truth vs. the world thing). Even w/o Brucato's stance on Orphans, MotA (Revised) IOC archmaster narrator answers the question of &quot;could be Orphan Archmages&quot; with a &quot;yes, of course&quot; (of sorts).<br /> <br /> Bottom line: I defend the narrative where Orphans have the same potential as...erm...&quot;institutionalized mages&quot;. *Having* to join in order to learn to do magick &quot;well&quot; it's a thing of the past. But I would <i>still </i>think that the <i>opportunity</i> of learning magick from mentors, books, temples, etc. it's an advantage of joining a faction. One that certainly does depend on Focus, but very few Focuses would reject in it's entirety","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-04-2021, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:00:23-07:00","id":1466665,"title":"","content":"On that note, I would also point out that while Mentors and Libraries are not unique to the Traditions, it is a heck of a lot easier to find one that's compatible with your Focus through the Traditions. So there's that. As you say, it's not such an overwhelming edge that mages need to join or else be excluded from the higher ranks of ability; but it's not nothing, either.<br /> <br /> I guess that my earlier pushback came from the fact that I was looking for carrots, and everyone was presenting me with sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-04-2021, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}